, and the rater consensus sits at Likely R with markets pricing the Democrat near 25%. A fresh Democratic-sponsored poll showing Johnson narrowly ahead and Cook's downgrade justify shading toward Lean R, but not past it.", "watch": "Independent polling confirming Johnson's competitiveness, or a favorable national environment for Democrats, would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Brad Finstad (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Brad Finstad seeks reelection in a southern Minnesota district that leans Republican by about six points. Democrat Jake Johnson has run an active campaign, touring all 21 counties and raising roughly as much money as the incumbent, and a late September poll from a Democratic sponsor showed him up by a point. Several ratings outlets, including Cook Political Report, have downgraded Finstad's standing, though most still rate the race Likely Republican.\n\nPrediction markets give Johnson about a one-in-four chance, and the district's fundamentals still favor the incumbent. The race looks like a Lean Republican contest with genuine upside risk for Democrats if the political environment breaks their way.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1904, "margin": -5.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.19, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1925, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3207, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2388, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2075, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.271, "margin": -4.0}]}